course: dictionary
lesson: 477
title: One word, many meanings: art
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word art has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. Read the clues before you choose. «Kintsugi is a Japanese art of mending broken pottery with gold.» Here an art is a skill that takes practice, like the art of cooking. You cannot hang a skill on a wall.
explain: Art can also mean making pictures, sculptures and other things that are beautiful or show ideas and feelings. When art means the things people have made, such as paintings in a gallery, the sentence will usually mention something you can see or visit. Ask yourself: is this about making something, the thing that was made, or a skill?
explain: When you see arts with an s, it usually means school subjects like music, dance, drama, painting and literature. At school, art is a lesson where pupils draw, paint and model clay. Context is the clue that tells you which meaning the writer chose.
fact: Art means making things that are beautiful or show ideas and feelings, like painting and drawing.
fact: Art can also mean the things people have made, such as paintings in a gallery.
fact: «An art» is a skill that takes practice, such as the art of cooking.
fact: «The arts» are subjects like music, dance, drama, painting and literature.
fact: An installation is art that fills a room, like Yayoi Kusama's Infinity Mirror Rooms, where mirrors and lights make the space look endless.
exercise: «Kintsugi is a Japanese art of mending broken pottery with gold.» In this sentence, what does art mean? | *A skill that takes practice | A painting hanging in a gallery | A school subject like music | A golden bowl on a shelf
exercise: «Infinity Mirror Rooms» are rooms where mirrors and lights make the space look endless. Find and copy the word that names art that fills a room. | artist | *installation | lights | mirror
exercise: «At school, art is a lesson where pupils draw, paint and model clay.» What does art mean in this sentence? | A picture sold for money | A broken bowl mended with gold | A skill like cooking | *A school subject where you draw and paint
test: «The arts» in this list: music, dance, drama, painting and literature. What do the arts mean here? | Pictures on a wall at home | Things made in a gallery | *Subjects that you can learn at school | A skill that takes lots of practice
test: «In 2022 a picture made with an AI tool won a digital art prize.» What kind of art does the prize celebrate? | The skill of cooking | A school lesson about clay | Pottery mended with gold | *Pictures and other beautiful things made on a computer
exam: Jayden says art only means paintings. Is he right? | Yes, art only ever means paintings in galleries | *No, art can mean a skill, the things made, or school subjects | No, art only means music and dance | Yes, but only when the picture is very old
